==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|state|ly}}. Compare {{l|en|stour}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsteɪtli/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stately.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|of [[person|people]]}} {{1|worthy}} of [[respect#Noun|respect]]; [[dignified#Adjective|dignified]], [[regal]].
#* '''1900''', {{w|Charles W. Chesnutt}}, ''The House Behind the Cedars'', Chapter I,
#*: Warwick's first glance had revealed the fact that the young woman was strikingly handsome, with a '''stately''' beauty seldom encountered.
# {{lb|en|of [[movement]]}} [[deliberate#Adjective|Deliberate]], [[unhurried]]; dignified.
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=An Own Goal on Gay Rights|newspaper={{w|The Economist}}|date=14 October 2010|passage=And much as they welcome his promise to repeal "don't ask, don't tell", they are dismayed by the '''stately''' pace and bungled tactics of his attempts to do so.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=Guadalcanal Campaign - Santa Cruz (IJN 2 : 2 USN)|date=3 February 2021|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xY2LC6Rz7JE|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221204001940/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xY2LC6Rz7JE|archivedate=4 December 2022|accessdate=11 December 2022|time=20:43|text=At about twenty past three in the afternoon, ''these'' aircraft duly began to arrive.  The cruiser ''Northampton'' was towing ''Hornet'' at a '''stately''' five knots when, out of the sky, came seven torpedo-armed aircraft.  They managed to ''miss'' the barely-moving ''Hornet'' with all but one drop... but one hit was really all that it took, the location causing additional damage to the stricken carrier and demolishing most of the repairs that had been made to the earlier damage.}}
# [[grand#Adjective|Grand]], [[impressive]], [[imposing#Adjective|imposing]].
#* {{RQ:Coleridge Christabel|page=55|passage=In Xanadu did {{smallcaps|Kubla Khan}} / A '''stately''' pleasure-dome decree: / Where {{smallcaps|Alph}}, the sacred river, ran / Through caverns measureless to man / Down to a sunless sea.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=December|author=Voyageur|title=The Mountain Railways of the Bernese Oberland|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=752|text=Below is the deep abyss of the Lauterbrunnen valley, and at its head a '''stately''' semi-circle of mountains, with the pyramidal Lauterbrunnen Breithorn as the centre-piece.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author={{w|John le Carré}} [pseudonym; David John Moore Cornwell]|title={{w|A Perfect Spy}}|year=1986|passage=Flora is a good scout, a favourite with the jockeys on account of her '''stately''' breasts and the generous use she puts them to.}}

